            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi!\r\n\r\n'mini.jump' implements five different mappings for initiating and performing jumps: `f`, `t`, `F`, `T`, and `;`. The idea is to start jumping with one of those (for example, `f`), type character to which user wants to jump (for example, `e`), and then keep jumping with one of those five keys. So like `feffFF` will initiate forward inclusive jumping to character `e`, repeat two those jumps, the perform two backward jumps.\r\n\r\nTo answer your questions:\r\n- I am not sure that you *really* want prompt for a new search on cursor moved. It will basically disable any other operation in Normal mode. `MiniJump.on_cursormoved()` is exported only to be used inside module's autocommand to reset jumping state. It shouldn't be used directly.\r\n- No, no reverse jump. The idea is for users to reverse jumping direction by typing same letter in another case: if jumping with `f`, then type `F` and keep jumping with `F`.",
